# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# Virtual environments
.venv

# SDD scratch: per-plan workspace for subagent-driven development
.superpowers/

# mutmut copies sources and tests here to mutate them; pytest and ruff
# would otherwise collect the copies and fail on the duplicates.
mutants/

# Local configuration. `.env` holds real values -- including
# AGENT_NEO4J_PASSWORD, which has no default and must not be committed.
# `.env.example` is the committed template; keep the two in step.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Worktrees live here. Only the worktrees -- the rest of `.claude/` is
# settings and agents somebody may well want tracked.
.claude/worktrees/

# --- frontend ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Installed packages and tool caches, and the built console itself.
#
# `research_team/interfaces/web/static/` was committed for a year, because it is
# what `uv run web.py` serves and committing it meant the web UI ran without a
# Node toolchain. That stopped paying: every branch that touched `frontend/src`
# rebuilt the same handful of chunk files, so any two such branches conflicted
# on bytes nobody reads or reviews, and the conflict had to be resolved by
# rebuilding rather than by reading. The cost of the swap is a prerequisite:
# `cd frontend && npm run build` before the console will serve.
node_modules/
research_team/interfaces/web/static/
frontend/.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
frontend/coverage/

# Vitest browser mode writes a PNG beside a failing test, which is genuinely
# useful while you are looking at one and is debris the moment it passes. The
# suite is local-only, so these would only ever be committed by accident.
frontend/src/**/__screenshots__/
# And a second directory for the same debris, which the previous commit missed
# because nothing had failed at the top level yet: the screenshot is written
# beside the test, and the attachment the reporter links to is written here.
frontend/.vitest-attachments/

# Subagent-driven-development scratch: ledgers, briefs and review packages
# for a plan in flight. Regenerated from the plan and git log, and meaningless
# once the branch lands -- the commits are the record.
.superpowers/
